    "finding": "The default-five-worker strict checks for PR #3067 and exact main took about 74 and 73 seconds. The PR emitted two rate-limit waits and main emitted one. Both passed with unchanged strict behavior. This pair shows the 120-second latency target can be met without a worker change, while rate-limit wait frequency still varies. The earlier PR #3066/main pair was about 133/254 seconds with four/three waits. This variance is consistent with an external service or concurrency effect but does not isolate worker count.",
